(Markus Kuhn: In the ISO paper size system, the height-to-width ratio of all pages is the square) Tj
T*
(root of two \(1.4142 : 1\). In other words, the width and the height of a page relate to each) Tj
T*
(other like the side and the diagonal of a square. This aspect ratio is especially convenient) Tj
T*
(for a paper size. If you put two such pages next to each other, or equivalently cut one) Tj
T*
(parallel to its shorter side into two equal pieces, then the resulting page will have again the) Tj
T*
(same width/height ratio. Same principle as the using the square root of 2 to achieve a very) Tj
T*
(similar aspect ratio on both the iPhone Duo?s inner and outer displays. With the international) Tj
T*
(paper system, you can do things like scale up 2× or scale down 0.5× without changing the) Tj
T*
(relative margins. E.g. print or photocopy at 50 percent to get two virtual pages per printed) Tj
T*
(page of output. It?s an elegant system. ?) Tj
